        <description> 
            The Optical Navigation (OpNav) camera is a Pixelink Prometheus PL-D725 camera hard-mounted on 
            the starboard lower side of the Crew Module Adapter (CMA) of the Artemis II Orion spacecraft. 
            The primary use of the OpNav camera is for spacecraft navigation during flight. It captured 
            images of the Earth and Moon during the Artemis II mission, complementing observations made 
            by other cameras onboard Orion.
        </description>
